          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "MATHEMATICS"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.138,
            0.9,
            0.174
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If Q(0, 1) is equidistant from "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{P}(5, -3)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { R } ( x ,   6 )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , find the values of x. Also find the distances QR and PR."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.179,
            0.901,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find a relation between x and y such that the point "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( x , y )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is equidistant from the point (3, 6) and (– 3, 4)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.235,
            0.324,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.3 Section Formula"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.263,
            0.517,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us recall the situation in Section 7.2. Suppose a telephone company wants to position a relay tower at P between A and B is such a way that the distance of the tower from B is twice its distance from A. If P lies on AB, it will divide AB in the ratio 1 : 2 (see Fig. 7.9). If we take A as the origin O, and 1 km as one unit on both the axis, the coordinates of B will be (36, 15). In order to know the position of the tower, we must know the coordinates of P. How do we find these coordinates?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.542,
            0.287,
            0.898,
            0.45
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.542,
                0.287,
                0.898,
                0.45
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.5,
            0.902,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let the coordinates of P be "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( x ,   y )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Draw perpendiculars from P and B to the x-axis, meeting it in D and E, respectively. Draw PC perpendicular to BE. Then, by the AA similarity criterion, studied in Chapter 6,   POD and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta   \\mathrm { B P C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are similar."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.564,
            0.579,
            0.608
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore , "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{OD}{PC} = \\frac{OP}{PB} = \\frac{1}{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{\\mathrm{PD}}{\\mathrm{BC}} = \\frac{\\mathrm{OP}}{\\mathrm{PB}} = \\frac{1}{2}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.613,
            0.451,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { x } { 3 6   -   x }   =   \\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{y}{15 - y} \\div \\frac{1}{2}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.656,
            0.482,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These equations give "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = 1 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = 5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.681,
            0.516,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You can check that P(12, 5) meets the condition that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{OP}:\\mathrm{PB}=1:2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.726,
            0.516,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now let us use the understanding that you may have developed through this example to obtain the general formula."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.788,
            0.517,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider any two points "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A } ( x _ { 1 } , y _ { 1 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathbf { B } ( x _ { _ 2 } ,   y _ { _ 2 } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and assume that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { ~ P ~ } ( x ,   y )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " divides AB internally in the ratio "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "m _ { _ 1 } : m _ { _ 2 } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " i.e., "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { \\mathrm { P A } } { \\mathrm { P B } }   =   \\frac { m _ { 1 } } { m _ { 2 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (see Fig. 7.10)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
